# Current theses

## Thesis T-migrated-adapters-meson: Preserve reviewed project guidance
Status: accepted
Based-on: user-reviewed-contract-migration

### Guidance
#### module Meson checkout integration adapter

Detect a consumer root `meson.build`. The lifecycle passes `Export.Path` as the
consumer-root-relative directory in the one submodule checkout. This adapter only connects that
directory and never creates, updates, copies, or removes a checkout.

#### decision One owned dependency region in the consumer build

Write sorted `subdir(Export.Path)` lines inside a marked region immediately after the root
`project()` statement, before consumer statements can use dependency variables. This keeps paths
consumer-root-relative, which Meson requires because `subdir` forbids `..`. Remove only the named
owned line and remove the region only when no managed dependency remains. Foreign bytes inside
the owned region are reported and canonically repaired; all bytes outside it remain untouched.

#### invariant One resolved submodule source tree

Read-only Capability rejects empty, `.`, absolute, and escaping paths as typed not-wirable. Meson
does not demand a second checkout under `subprojects/`; the owned region references the shared
submodule source directly. Pull configures it in `.git-a2a/build/meson` without compiling the
whole consumer. Remove reconfigures when managed Meson dependencies remain; removing the last
one deletes the adapter-owned setup tree so consumer references to the intentionally removed
dependency do not block removal. Inspect reports both declaration drift and a missing checkout.
Commit selection and checkout ownership remain with the submodule adapter.

#### test Golden lifecycle

Tests cover private editor idempotence, Inspect, read-only Capability, missing checkouts,
foreign-content repair, removal restoring root bytes, sorted lines, and unrelated entries.

### Rationale
Migrated from the pre-2.0 HINT source format without changing its guidance.

